From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weiyi Feng <fwy1998@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:01:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hosted: Beringia host calls, console and panic report

beringia_hook (set by the loader) marks a hosted kernel; beringia_call() is
the host-call entry. The serial driver becomes the host console when hosted
(kprintf and the serial console), and panic_trap_to_debugger hands the
formatted message to the host, which ends the run.
---
 EXTERNAL_HEADERS/beringia_hosted.h |  67 ++++++++++++++++++
 osfmk/conf/files.x86_64            |   1 +
 osfmk/kern/debug.c                 |  21 ++++++
 osfmk/x86_64/beringia.c            | 107 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pexpert/i386/pe_serial.c           |  29 ++++++++
 5 files changed, 225 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 EXTERNAL_HEADERS/beringia_hosted.h
 create mode 100644 osfmk/x86_64/beringia.c

